WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.045
Motivation is social as well as individual.

2
00:00:03.045 --> 00:00:10.442
Norms, accountability, recognition, leadership signals, peer support, shared goals, and feedback culture all influence effort and persistence.

3
00:00:10.442 --> 00:00:13.922
People watch what the group treats as normal.

4
00:00:13.922 --> 00:00:18.708
They also watch what leaders praise, ignore, measure, interrupt, or punish.

5
00:00:18.708 --> 00:00:28.279
A team can make good work easier to continue, or it can quietly drain motivation from the work it claims to value.

6
00:00:28.279 --> 00:00:34.805
Social accountability can support follow-through when it is respectful and connected to shared goals.

7
00:00:34.805 --> 00:00:44.812
It works best when expectations are clear, progress is visible, and people can ask for help before a small issue becomes a failure.

8
00:00:44.812 --> 00:00:49.162
Recognition also matters when it points to behaviors worth repeating.

9
00:00:49.162 --> 00:00:55.688
Specific recognition teaches the team what good work looks like more effectively than vague praise.

10
00:00:55.688 --> 00:01:04.825
Psychological safety at a practical level means people can ask questions, surface problems, and admit uncertainty without being punished for honesty.

11
00:01:04.825 --> 00:01:07.435
This does not mean lowering standards.

12
00:01:07.435 --> 00:01:13.091
It means creating a climate where problems become visible early enough to solve.

13
00:01:13.091 --> 00:01:21.357
Shame-based pressure can force short-term compliance, but it often hides confusion, encourages defensive behavior, and damages learning.

14
00:01:21.357 --> 00:01:25.273
Teams should not depend only on heroic individual motivation.

15
00:01:25.273 --> 00:01:33.974
If the system requires people to constantly overcome confusion, conflicting priorities, broken tools, and invisible progress, motivation will eventually suffer.

16
00:01:33.974 --> 00:01:38.760
Better team systems make important work easier to start and continue.

17
00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:46.156
They clarify priorities, reduce unnecessary friction, support recovery, and build momentum through shared direction and useful feedback.
